{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban use of environmentally harmful non-biodegradable materials at public events",
        "additional_details": "Public events should be able to take place without causing unnecessary harm to wildlife, animals and the environment. Examples include festivals, fairs, parades and other outdoor gatherings where materials such as plastic glitter, synthetic confetti or similar non-biodegradable decorations may be used. These can pollute habitats, enter waterways and pose risks to animals. This petition calls for national standards requiring event organisers on public land to use environmentally safe alternatives where available and prevent avoidable pollution.",
        "background": "I ask the Government to introduce rules to prevent the use and release of environmentally harmful materials, such as plastic glitter and synthetic confetti, at public events held on public land, and require organisers to use safe, environmentally responsible alternatives to help protect wildlife.",
